## State Encoded in Types

### The Problem

```xiom
pub type Connection = {
  host: Str;
  is_connected: Bool;
}

impl Connection {
  fn send(self: &Connection, data: Str) {
    // Runtime check — easy to forget!
    if !self.is_connected { panic("Not connected"); }
  }
}
```

### The Type State Solution

```xiom
pub type Connection[State] = {
  host: Str;
  state: State;
}

pub type Disconnected = {};
pub type Connected = { fd: Int; }

impl Connection[Disconnected] {
  fn new(host: Str) -> Connection[Disconnected] {
    return Connection{ host: host, state: Disconnected{} };
  }

  fn connect(self: Connection[Disconnected]) -> Connection[Connected] {
    let fd = os.connect(self.host);
    return Connection{ host: self.host, state: Connected{ fd: fd } };
  }
}

impl Connection[Connected] {
  fn send(self: &Connection[Connected], data: Str) {
    os.write(self.state.fd, data);  // Safe: we know we're connected
  }

  fn close(self: Connection[Connected]) -> Connection[Disconnected] {
    os.close(self.state.fd);
    return Connection{ host: self.host, state: Disconnected{} };
  }
}

fn main() {
  let conn = Connection::new("localhost");   // Disconnected
  let conn = conn.connect();                   // Connected
  conn.send("Hello");                          // Works!
  let conn = conn.close();                     // Disconnected
  // conn.send("World");                       // COMPILE ERROR!
}
```

### Type State Transitions

```
New → Disconnected → Connected → Disconnected → Dropped
       ↑_____________________________|
```

Each state is a different type — only valid operations are available. Calling send() on a Disconnected connection is a compile error, not a runtime panic.

### Phantom State

```xiom
pub type File[State] = {
  path: Str;
  _state: PhantomData[State];  // Zero-size marker, not stored at runtime
}

pub type Open = {};
pub type Closed = {};
```

The state type parameter is consumed at compile time — zero runtime overhead.

### Multi-Step Builder

```xiom
let burger = Burger::new()       // Empty burger
  .add_bun()                     // BurgerWithBun
  .add_patty()                   // BurgerWithPatty
  .add_cheese()                  // BurgerWithCheese
  .add_lettuce()                 // BurgerReady
  .build();                      // Burger (can't skip steps!)
```

